```java
@Service // still a singleton, now safe
public class OrderService {
    public void process(String user) {
        save(user); // user stays in a local/param: one copy per call
    }

    private void save(String user) { /* persist */ }
}
```
Local variables live on each thread's stack, so passing per-request data as parameters keeps a shared singleton thread-safe.

